# ENDCT3 - Missing END Before Keyword

...

## What this rule does

Reports when a block-opening keyword starts before the previous block has been
closed with `end`. This typically means an inner `end` was consumed by an inner
construct, leaving the outer construct without its closing `end`.

## Examples

### Incorrect

```matlab
if x
    for i = 1:10
        y = i;
    end
% missing 'end' for 'if' — the 'end' closed the 'for' instead
```

### Correct

```matlab
